    {
      "id": "-IwzL3_q56hVOsgM2vRar",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1554.1661386839228,
      "y": 1662.6674794585517,
      "width": 438.159912109375,
      "height": 180,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5E",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 779178301,
      "version": 947,
      "versionNonce": 695866899,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1777155576267,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "We will have another set of producers, called the \nworkers, who will pull of the raw events from Kafka\nand execute atomic increment commands.\nLike if a user likes a video, the data would be put\nto the Redis cluster,\nThis Redis cluster acts as a ultra fast write coalescing\nlayer, absorbing the rapid increment commands from the\nworkers and handle write spikes, like viral video\ngetting 100K likes in 5 seconds ",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "We will have another set of producers, called the \nworkers, who will pull of the raw events from Kafka\nand execute atomic increment commands.\nLike if a user likes a video, the data would be put\nto the Redis cluster,\nThis Redis cluster acts as a ultra fast write coalescing\nlayer, absorbing the rapid increment commands from the\nworkers and handle write spikes, like viral video\ngetting 100K likes in 5 seconds ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
